# Ducking Gravity Architect

Run as a **separate** `generalPurpose` Task during **ARCHITECT** (never the implementer self-certifying). Prefer **`cursor-grok-4.6-high-fast`** → **`cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast`** → omit `model`. Do **not** use Opus/Sonnet for this gate unless the user explicitly asks. Stay **local** — `.cursor/rules/prefer-local-agents.mdc`. Cost chains: `.cursor/rules/subagent-watchdog.mdc`.

**Why Grok 4.6 High (aligned with SmartAstro 8/18/2026):** this gate used to prefer Sonnet with an Opus fallback. Those slugs cost far more per token than Cursor Grok 4.6 High and did not change the merge-ready bar. Architect still runs as a **separate Task** from implement; it just must not burn premium tokens.

## Check against

- Acceptance criteria fully met; no scope creep
- `.cursor/rules/marketing-sync.mdc` invariants (popup vs managed tables, `removedScheduleIds`, Class Over)
- `.cursor/rules/architecture.mdc` placement (Netlify `lib/` vs browser JS)
- Tests cover the risky date/sync edge cases
- No secrets committed; minimal diffs

## Verdict

- **Merge-ready** — list residual risks (if any) that are acceptable
- **Blockers** — concrete fixes required; pipeline rewinds to **BUGBOT** after implementer fixes

Companion SmartAstro sender contract: `earthboundtrev/astro` `docs/integrations/marketing-site-sync.md` when sync behavior changed.
